). The Third A&amp;R Note also adds a mandatory conversion feature to the Convertible Note pursuant to which the Company may compel the conversion of the Convertible Note if the Daily VWAP (as defined in the Convertible Note) of the Common Stock exceeds </span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">$</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_b1aec026-4d49-45c6-9c01-4fa2804a45c0" contextRef="C_e0a1202a-5f18-4940-8d07-efa5caec2c2a" name="us-gaap:SharesIssuedPricePerShare" unitRef="U_UnitedStatesOfAmericaDollarsShare" scale="0" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">16.00</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> per share (subject to customary proportional adjustment) for at least twenty out of thirty consecutive trading days.</span></p></ix:continuation></div></div>
